// spec: EXP-013
//
// Positional arguments come first and named ones after -- Python's rule.  A
// positional argument following a named one is refused.
//
// ⚠️ This is also what spares absorption a rule of its own [FUN-005].  Gathering
// takes trailing POSITIONAL arguments, and positional arguments end exactly
// where naming begins, so the two features never have to negotiate.

procedure Log (Level : String, Message : String);
begin
    WriteLn (Level + ': ' + Message);
end

Log (Level: 'warn', 'disk');
